<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mariano IV of Arborea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1317–1376</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mariano IV was judge (ruler) of Arborea in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> from 1347 to 1376. At first an ally of the Crown of Aragon, he turned against it in 1353 and fought to drive the Aragonese from Sardinia, bringing most of the island under his control. His daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-arborea">Eleanor of Arborea</a> continued the struggle and issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carta-de-logu">Carta de Logu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mariano-iv-of-arborea.jpg" alt="Mariano IV of Arborea" width="320" height="494" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariano_IV_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
